  "description": "Native-boundary isolation seam for ToolUp companions — runs a native parser (Tesseract, SkiaSharp, Verovio, any P/Invoke-backed companion) over UNTRUSTED bytes in a sacrificial child process behind a narrow binary pipe, so a crash in the native layer is a typed refusal (WorkerCrashed / TimedOut / MemoryCapExceeded) rather than host-process code execution. In-process stays the default for trusted input; the seam is opt-in per path and mandatory under the verified composition profile. BCL only, no vendor SDK. Server-only companion.",
